        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "aff96541-fe54-5dbf-afbb-8101925dc847",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Catuaba infusions, Brazilian drinks, herbal medicine\n- Plants: Erythroxylum vacciniifolium, trees native to Brazil\n- Languages: Guarani, Paraguayan Guarani\n- Concepts: Guarani word meanings, Tupi–Guarani language family\n\nFacts:\n- Catuaba is the name used for infusions made from the bark of several trees native to Brazil.\n- The word Catuaba comes from Guarani and means “what gives strength to the Indian.”\n- Guarani is an indigenous language of South America, and its primary variety is Paraguayan Guarani, whose endonym is \"avañe'ẽ\" meaning “the people's language.”\n- Guarani belongs to the Tupi–Guarani family within the Tupian languages.\n- Erythroxylum vacciniifolium is also known as Catuaba.\n- Erythroxylum vacciniifolium is used as an aphrodisiac in Brazilian drinks and herbal medicine.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
